  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "PDURATION evaluates (LN(fv) - LN(pv)) / LN(1 + rate) rather than LN(fv / pv), drifting 22 ULP at 0.025",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20326 through 20527, PDURATION(rate, pv, fv) rejects nonpositive rate, pv, or fv with #NUM! and computes (LN(fv) - LN(pv)) / LN(1 + rate) via Excel's x87 LN chain instead of LN(fv / pv) / LN(1 + rate). On =PDURATION(0.025,2000,2200), this yields 3.859866162622655 (0x400ee10182bb35e8), 22 ULP above the exact mathematical value. In compatibility version 1, @PDURATION returns #NAME?.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20430 (1,205/1,205 full-bank and 120/120 pinned PDURATION rows) and 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 378).",
